{
 "id": "move:trillion-sweep-scripts-to-apps",
 "about": "The old-trillion sweep, scripts lane: every file under scripts/ (and the tests in test/ that reach them) still only on old trillion main 5dc302be37 with no copy in a new repository, carried byte for byte into trillion-apps web/, which keeps the old web app's own paths under it (web/scripts, web/test), beside the build, deploy and check code already there. They are the old app's own build, deploy, release, proof and repository-guard scripts, so they belong with the app (engine-feature-boundary.json: screens, app parts and their release/build/deploy scripts are trillion-apps). One group per file, so a file whose import has no home yet is held alone. Files whose import is home in the Workshop package import it there; files a newer copy here already adapted are adapted_homes. src/typed-operation-contract.mjs comes too, as old main held it, into web/src: the Workshop's newer tools/shared-code copy imports a .ts file that Node will not strip under node_modules, so the scripts that import it cannot load it from the package.",
